### What is the expected behavior?

For a standard Responses request with no available tools, omit `tool_choice` so a strict compatible provider can perform text-only summarization. Requests with available tools should retain their existing tool-selection behavior.

### Additional information

**Source-level root cause:** the same construction is present on current `main` at commit `5c5308fc9a9ee789049d646ef11e5400384b9c6f`:

- [Local compaction creates a default Prompt with no tools](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/5c5308fc9a9ee789049d646ef11e5400384b9c6f/codex-rs/core/src/compact.rs#L287-L290).
- [The standard Responses path serializes the prompt's tool list](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/5c5308fc9a9ee789049d646ef11e5400384b9c6f/codex-rs/core/src/client.rs#L915-L920).
- [The request builder unconditionally assigns `tool_choice: "auto"`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/5c5308fc9a9ee789049d646ef11e5400384b9c6f/codex-rs/core/src/client.rs#L966-L975).
- [`ResponsesApiRequest.tool_choice` is a nonoptional String](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/5c5308fc9a9ee789049d646ef11e5400384b9c6f/codex-rs/codex-api/src/common.rs#L259-L269).

**Live workaround and verification:** in my xAI transport adapter, omitting only `tool_choice` when tools are absent, null, or an empty array allowed the original conversation to complete compaction and resume. Two resumed turns completed successfully with CLI exit 0. A separate minimal streaming request returned HTTP 200, model `grok-4.6`, the expected text, and a real `response.completed` event. The adapter preserves nonempty tools and their selection setting.

The standalone reproduction above bypasses that adapter and demonstrates the current CLI request shape independently of xAI authentication or my existing session history.

**Possible fix direction:** make tool-choice serialization conditional on the logical availability of tools. Please account for Responses Lite, where tool declarations can be embedded in input rather than the top-level `tools` field; this report reproduces the standard Responses/custom-provider path. Suggested regression coverage is an empty-tool local-compaction request accepted by a strict mock, plus unchanged behavior for a nonempty tool list.
